#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""End-to-end QA of the Lani app on an Android emulator.

Starts the emulator (AVD "lani-qa", or "fluent-qa" made before the rename; $LANI_QA_AVD) if needed, builds and installs a fresh debug APK (--minified: the qa build, R8 as in a release), runs the
dev bridge on a COPY of the learner data, drives the main flows by visible text, takes a screenshot
per step and fails on crashes. Real learner data is never touched.

A second town to visit: a fixture Italian town (companion/bridge/test/fixtures/dev-town.json, the Friuli
culture pack) on its own dev bridge (test/dev-town.ts, a temp data dir), linked with the dev bridge's town;
the visit steps go to it from Friends and back home.

Usage: companion/bin/qa [--no-build] [--minified | --apk <file>] [--keep-bridge] [--no-town] [--steps <names>] [--happening <scene>/<id>] [--dry] [--bridges-only]
  --minified           the qa build instead of the debug build (:app:assembleQa, app-qa.apk): the release build's R8, with
                       its rules and optimizations, and QA's hooks, the debug build's manifest (the dev bridge over plain
                       HTTP), x86_64 and the debug key (app/build.gradle.kts); a crash or a screen that loads nothing
                       there is a keep rule missing (app/proguard-rules.pro). Not debuggable: QA reads the app's
                       files with the emulator's su instead of run-as
  --apk <file>         install that APK, built nothing (a debug or qa build: a release build has neither QA's hooks
                       nor plain HTTP to the dev bridge)
  --steps visit,packs  only these steps (and setup); "visit" is Friends and every visit step (with "town-progress": the
                       second town's "📈 Napredek · Progress" from its card, a hard word's challenge sent, then just the
                       village shared with it; LANI_DEV_TOWN_FIXTURE=dev-town-child.json makes the second town a child's
                       with a learner's progress, the dev bridge's town its guardian, and LANI_DEV_DATA a synthetic
                       parent: bun test/fixtures/make-learner.ts <dir>); "town-progress-child" (named only, last) pairs
                       the app with that child's town: its Friends with "👪 Tvoj starš vidi tvoj napredek", the parent's
                       progress seen as just the village; "road" the car's
                       "🚗 Za pot" (a small library got ready, played, next, paused; "❓ Kviz": a pick by next, a
                       question again by previous; browsed as Android Auto does: two tabs, each session played);
                       "scene-building" a building's scene (the hut's kitchen, a house's room …) with the building in
                       its top bar, its card opened from there, its words' run and back to the card in the scene;
                       "fire-peek" hide-and-seek by the fire: the children hidden behind the stump, peeking out at a
                       wrong guess, found (QA's hook "happening:ob-ognju/lovljenje/lovljenje-skrivalnice"); "field-cues"
                       the cues of the field, the tower, the market and the pond: the hare startled out of the grass,
                       the pedlar on the road, the hen on the cart (a tap turn), Muri barking by the jetty, each dialog
                       opened through the hook and played to its cue; "sheets-settle" flings into the end of Home, the
                       tutor chat's sheet and the challenges' sheet, each still a second later (no endless bounce);
                       "cheat-sheet" the cheat sheet ("📋 Plonk listek") from Home, from an exercise
                       of imeti-in-iti (its card first) and a tutor message with a list pinned in the chat (QA's
                       hook "chat:table"), the dev bridge's village keeping it; "chat-swipe" a tutor message
                       (QA's hook "chat:<text>") swiped in the chat: its tip shown once, to the right the reply card,
                       to the left bookmarked (its 🔖, the snackbar), again to the left taken away and undone, a drag
                       down on a message scrolling the list (the sheet stays); its long press's "📄 Kopiraj" and
                       "↗️ Deli" (the share sheet); "chat-links" a tutor message's links (QA's hook "chat:<text>"):
                       example.com's asks first ("🔗 Odpreti example.com?", Cancel), an http one too ("⚠️ Povezava ni
                       varna"), fran.si's opens at once (the browser in front, then the app again); "chat-attach" 💬 in
                       an exercise's top bar (imeti-in-iti): the exercise attached above the input before the answer, its
                       ✕, the answer with it after; "chat-attach-pack" 💬 by a pack's word: "📎 <word> = <meaning>";
                       "chat-photo" a photo in the chat: a sign with GPS EXIF put in the emulator's gallery (taken away
                       after), 📷 → the photo picker, sent with a line of text, its thumbnail, full screen and zoomed,
                       the dev bridge's copy keeping it under app/chat-images/ upright, 1568 px, without EXIF (mode 0600),
                       the chat event's image (bridge.log), deleted from its long press (on the node too); then 📷 → the
                       camera (allowed when asked), the virtual scene taken and sent alone;
                       "typed-turn" a dialog's turn typed with the keyboard up (QA's hook "turns:type"), the
                       keyboard the answer's (its language, no suggestion strip); "player-voice" the learner's voice in
                       Babica's soup: a choice tapped said in it before her reply (tag Speaker, player-voice.log), its
                       line's 🔊, a turn by the 🎤 (QA's hook "mic:right") not said again, a turn typed right said; "ispy" a game of «Vidim, vidim» by
                       the fire (QA's hook "ispy:ob-ognju/stump"): a wrong thing tapped, the right one, the child's
                       lines in turn (tags Speaker and Voice: each clip played to its end before the next line,
                       ispy-speech.log), a second game left mid-line (its clip stopped);
                       "scene-people" I spy offered in the church, the kitchen and the smithy (QA's hook "ispy:"):
                       who stands where, the picture as it opens and closer up; the church's top bar with the base
                       in German ("‹ Vas · Dorf"), its pills apart, then the profile's pair again;
                       "your-words" a dialog that tests the learner's own words answered right, its end listing them;
                       "word-missed" one got wrong first, its card after the turn; "project-step" the maypole's first
                       step as its scene (QA's hook "step:mlaj/1"): the sheet, the forest, the tap turn, the step done;
                       then one over the village (the chapel's first, else the maypole's third); "scene-coherence"
                       what a dialog says happens shows: the mill's last step (QA's hook "step:mlin/6": the wheel dry,
                       then turning as Tine says the water runs, the mill grinding), Luka's flock at the water (QA's hook
                       "happening:ob-potoku/ovce/ovce-stejem": coming, counted, going home); "age-up" an age's
                       moment (QA's hook "ageup:vas", then "ageup:trg"), held beat by beat ("ageup:at:<s>"), its card with
                       what's new, the party at A1 ("level:A1", "hour:19") to its end, the chronicle's "🎉 Poglej spet ·
                       Watch again"; "maypole-season"
                       the maypole on the map and on the square on 10 May (up) and 30 October (down; QA's hook
                       "season:<day>"); "kopa" the charcoal pile over real days (QA's hooks "kopa:<stage>",
                       "show:kopa", "hour:<h>"): each stage's pile on the map (the felled beech, the stack, the
                       smoke white, yellow, blue, the sacks, between piles, the winter), Miha's talk at two stages
                       with the pile over it, the night watch's breakout covered and missed (the ash after), Tone's
                       card on a delivery's day; "bridges" the crossing on the map at the stream bank (QA's hook
                       "show:riverbank") and closer up: the stepping stones before the bridge (QA's hook "step:most/1"),
                       the bridge half built ("step:most/4") and in the stream's scene, the bridge built
                       ("step:most/7": the project finished) by day, by night, the whole village and the scene; "trade" food for wood ("⇄ Zamenjaj · Trade"): the sheet, its run to the end,
                       the result, the HUD's stocks moved and the dev bridge's village keeping the day's trade;
                       "village-life" the village's day on the map (QA's hook "hour:<h>", which the map follows too):
                       zoomed in at 8, 11, 15 and 19 o'clock (the people at their chores and work about the village,
                       a few at a place, a couple at the fire by day, a handful in the evening), and the field beside
                       the fire at the moments someone walks by it ($LANI_QA_FIELD_WALK, "h:mm[:ss],…"; "9:25,11:02,12:30"
                       when unset);
                       "reactions" the people reacting to the village's events (QA's hooks "event:<kind>", "event:won",
                       "hour:<h>", "show:<spot>"): wolves coming and there by day (the defenders in the gate, the lookout,
                       the fire's gathering), a villager's card then (their line, "🐺 Branimo vas!", no talk), wolves at
                       night (torches), the cheer after a won fight, the bear, a storm, the merchant's cart, a feast day;
                       also as react-*.png in $LANI_QA_REACT_SHOTS;
                       "quests-threat" the requests during a threat and a drill whose task is passed, on a synthetic
                       learner with Vinar Marko's wine request passed and the drill for it open (LANI_DEV_DATA): the map
                       with the requests' bubbles, the wolves on (QA's hook "event:wolves/2") with none, the Scroll's
                       villagers with them waiting ("🐺 Po volkovih"), Home's strip with "Branimo vas" first, the bubbles
                       back after, Marko's card with the drill under Later ("✓ Naloga je opravljena: za vajo"); also as
                       quests-*.png in $LANI_QA_QUESTS_SHOTS;
                       "wishlist" the tutor's wishlist in the app: a select-all with its checkboxes and the count on
                       Check ("0 izbranih", "Preveri · Check (2)"), a choice's and a picked scenario's near miss (almost:
                       "Skoraj!"), a request's grammar card as a flashcard in its challenge (QA's hook "request:<ids>"); the
                       module and the cards written into the dev bridge's copy; also as wish-*.png in $LANI_QA_WISH_SHOTS;
                       "hearths" the hearths (QA's hooks "hearths:<age>", "hearths:short", "hearths:lit",
                       "hearths:feast", "hearths:cold", "hour:<h>", "kopa:sekanje", "show:kopa"): the camp's campfire,
                       the hamlet's first houses smoking, the village's fire ring by day and lit for the evening, its warm
                       windows and the forge at night, a wood shortage (the outlying houses dark, the HUD's 🔥 tile red,
                       its sheet), the square's fire basket and its kres on a feast evening, the town's lanterns, the
                       forge cold, Oglar Miha waiting for the village's wood (his talk, the sheet's line of the
                       pile's wood); also as hearths-*.png in
                       $LANI_QA_HEARTHS_SHOTS;
                       "storm" the storm and who is where (QA's hooks "event:storm", "event:wolves/2", "hour:11",
                       "show:fire"; a synthetic learner with the whole cast moved in, LANI_DEV_DATA): the map in the rain
                       (streaks, wet paths, puddles), a flash caught (the brightest sky of screenshots over 25 s of the
                       village's clock at a quarter: "clock:0.25"), Stari Janez's
                       living room with Janez and Lovec Jože at home and the rain on its window, "Danes tukaj" with
                       "⛈️ Nevihta", a tap on one: their line for inside; the kitchen; the field in the rain; the wolves
                       and the fire's scene with the children and the old gathered; also as storm-*.png in
                       $LANI_QA_STORM_SHOTS;
                       "coast" Teo's coast (a synthetic learner of the Friuli culture without a village, LANI_DEV_DATA;
                       the dev bridge's LANI_CULTURE=friuli and LANI_LANDSCAPE=coast; the phone in sl · en,
                       LANI_QA_PAIR=sl-en; LANI_QA_FOUND_SEED=551323397 founds at Teo's land, QA's hook "seed:<n>"): the
                       founding's preview, the village after founding with the sea and the beach in its first look, dragged
                       to the beach, closer at the sea's horizon by night, at dusk and by day, a wild animal tapped (its card in Italian), a villager's free talk in it · de (its
                       goals in Italian and German), the same land as a village and a town ("hearths:vas", "hearths:mesto");
