  --bridges-only       no app: start both bridges, link them, check what a visit asks through the dev bridge, stop
  --no-town            no second town (the visit steps are skipped)
  --happening ob-ognju/roke  that happening counts as on from the village on (QA's hook), so its person stands at its
                       place for the village's steps (Luka warming his hands at the fire: the fire's card and zoom with
                       someone beside it); a dialog step lets it go again
Output: companion/qa-shots/<timestamp>/  (NN-step.png, contact-sheet.png, report.txt, bridge.log, town.log)
Env: ANDROID_SERIAL picks the device when several run; LANI_DEV_PORT the dev bridge's port (default 8791);
LANI_PIPER_CACHE the dev bridge's offline voices (default ~/.cache/lani-qa/piper, kept between runs: the voice is fetched
from Hugging Face once), LANI_PIPER_URL where it fetches them (default Hugging Face; a local mirror of its layout);
LANI_DEV_TOWN_PORT the second town's (default 8797); LANI_DEV_TOWN_FIXTURE its fixture (a file of
companion/bridge/test/fixtures; default dev-town.json, with visit-voices dev-town-sl.json); LANI_DEV_DATA the data
the dev bridge copies (default: the default learner's, LANI_DATA_DIR in lani.env, else data/; with visit-voices a synthetic
Italian learner); LANI_DEV_FAKE_ELEVENLABS=1 a fake ElevenLabs for the dev bridge (clips made on demand end to end:
test/dev-bridge.ts); LANI_QA_VISIT_PAIR the phone's pair on a visit (QA's hook "pair:<t>-<b>", asked on Friends;
visit-voices: it-de unless set).
"""
import atexit
